 "input": "extension planning application, what the council does. you submit on the planning portal with drawings, site plan and the fee. council validates it (checks the paperwork, can ask for missing bits). once valid, case officer gets it, neighbours are consulted by letter and a site notice goes up, 21 days for comments. officer does a site visit and checks it against the local plan policies. they write the officer report with a recommendation. most householder ones are decided under delegated powers, controversial ones go to planning committee. decision notice issued, if refused you can appeal to the planning inspectorate.",
 "expect_status": "ok",
